   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ מַאי טַעְמָא? הַאי נְפִישׁ טִירְחֵיהּ, וְהַאי לָא נְפִישׁ טִירְחֵיהּ.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» that the Sages in Yavne said that Ila could take a wage of four issar for issuing a ruling concerning a small animal but six issar for issuing a ruling concerning a large animal? The Gemara answers: Examining «this» one, a firstborn of a large animal, for blemishes involves «great effort; but» examining «that» one, the firstborn of a small animal, does «not» involve such «great effort.»"
  }
